= May 2026 — A former president gets a studio

**Krzysztof Stanowski**, the journalist, Kanał Zero founder and former
presidential candidate, is turning his online audience into a television
institution. <span class="party-pis"><b>Andrzej Duda</b></span>, now a former President, will have his own
programme there. Neither man commands a parliamentary club, but together they
can decide which arguments and successors enter millions of homes as ordinary
conversation rather than party propaganda.

Lewica comes to the decision with a history: **[+ media_relationship +]**.
Kanał Zero helped set the terms of the 2025 presidential campaign, so this is
not a first interview request. We must decide whether to treat a frequently
hostile broadcaster as a permanent institution, build distribution of our own,
or refuse Stanowski the right to make an empty chair speak for us.

[? if pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = 1: In 2025 the audience became votes:
Stanowski reached **[+ pres_2025_r1_display_stanowski +]%** and left the count
with the support signal from which a party can be built. This television launch
is therefore the institutional sequel to a breakthrough, not a former
candidate finding another format.?]

- @zero_engage_2026
- @zero_build_2026
- @zero_boycott_2026

@zero_engage_2026
title: Maintain a prepared rotation of Left guests
subtitle: Pay for briefing, rehearsal and rapid rebuttal so no single interview becomes the whole party's media line. Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The media team cannot sustain another format.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_relationship = "Permanent prepared rotation through creator media"; media_capacity += 5; public_trust += 2; kanal_zero_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left treats Zero as a permanent institution rather than one hostile host"

A rota of MPs, trade-union economists and local organisers begins passing
through the studio with the same briefing book and a rapid-response team behind
it. Kanał Zero gains credible adversaries and more reach; Lewica gains the less
glamorous habit of surviving a hostile interview without letting one guest
invent the party line.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the first guest

@zero_build_2026
title: Answer television with a federated Left media network
subtitle: Put union, local and creator outlets on a shared distribution system without making them a central party channel. Cost: 3 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: The network cannot be capitalised.
on-arrival: resources -= 3; media_relationship = "Federated Left television, local and creator network"; rownosc_media_active = 1; media_capacity += 10; local_network += 3; public_trust += 2; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Równość celebrates the new Left media network as a broadcaster for tenants, workers and organisers"

Lewica pays for cameras, editing and distribution that local, union and
independent creators can share. The result is not a red Kanał Zero under a
party secretary: each outlet keeps its voice. That independence broadens the
audience, while **Równość**, a friendly hard-left outlet, treats the launch as
long-delayed vindication and immediately fills its first segments with praise
for a broadcaster finally built around tenants, workers and organisers. A
quarrel among regional barons over whose
programme gets the best slot.

- @poland_event_queue: Buy the equipment

@zero_boycott_2026
title: Refuse a channel that has become part of right-wing succession
subtitle: Deny the guest and accept that Stanowski will fill the segment, the clip and much of the young audience without us.
on-arrival: media_relationship = "Boycott of the creator-right ecosystem"; progressive_credibility += 2; media_capacity -= 3; kanal_zero_capacity += 4; young_support -= 2; news_headline = "The empty chair remains available for commentary"

No Lewica politician enters the studio. Stanowski turns the refusal into an
empty-chair segment, then lets Duda and invited commentators explain what the
Left would supposedly have said. The boycott is morally clear, commercially
useful to the channel and almost invisible to younger viewers who encounter
politics through its clips.

- @poland_event_queue: Decline the invitation

