Kosiniak-Kamysz offers another negotiation around hospital access, tenancy and
inheritance, with the most contested provisions stripped out. Lewica secures a
date for the revised text instead of accepting a promise to revisit it someday.
PSL deputies return to the table; equality organisations ask how many times a
basic civil status can be reduced before nothing remains.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the table

@partnership_failed_movement
title: Withdraw the compromise and rebuild a marriage-equality coalition
subtitle: Stop reducing the text for parliamentary arithmetic and organise around equal marriage instead.
view-if: partnership_sejm_passed = 0
on-arrival: partnership_strategy = "Movement rebuild for marriage equality"; progressive_credibility += 6; feminist_trust += 3; organiser_energy += 4; psl_relation -= 8; party_unity += 2; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += -8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 9; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 6; news_headline = "Lewica trades an immediate compromise for a broader equality campaign"

Kotula withdraws the failed compromise from the centre of Lewica's strategy and
invites equality organisations to write the next campaign around marriage
itself. There is no new law and no second vote waiting in committee. PSL leaves
the negotiating room; organisers who felt used as bargaining scenery finally
receive ownership of the next demand.

- @poland_event_queue: Hand the demand back to the organisers

@safe_financing_veto_2026
