= May 2026 — A veto with a delivery date attached

The act sets up how Poland draws and spends its share of the European defence
financing instrument: which ministry contracts, how the loans are recorded
against the deficit, which domestic firms qualify, and what the audit trail
looks like. It passed with the coalition's ordinary majority. President <span class="party-pis"><b>[+
president_name +]</b></span> vetoes it.

The stated reason is sovereignty over defence procurement. The practical
effect is that the ammunition, drone and air-defence contracts written against
that money cannot be signed on the current schedule, and the firms that hired
for them are told to wait. Overriding a veto needs three-fifths of a voting
Sejm; the coalition does not have it without help it has no reason to expect.

This is now the **[+ president_veto_count +]** veto of the term. Some of the
earlier ones were about courts and about who may marry. This one is about
whether the army receives equipment in 2027, which is a different kind of
argument and reaches a different set of voters.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Our ministers have to explain a defence
programme they cannot fund and did not block.?][? if left_in_government = 0:
We are outside the cabinet and can decide whether a defence veto is a fight
worth lending our votes to.?]
[? if mentzen_kingmaker_active = 1: The referendum lock on European defence
arrangements was point three of the declaration both finalists were handed
before the runoff. One of them signed it and is now President.?]
[? if parliament_visibility >= 55: The chamber still draws the audience it
found in 2023, which means an override roll call is watched rather than
reported.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem's caucus is not automatically on
the side of a rearmament bill and will say so in public.?][? if
left_dominant_current = "social_patriot": Our patriotic wing wants to own the
defence-delivery argument outright and take it into working-class towns.?]

[? if pension_defence_credit >= 4: We are the only party in this chamber that
answered PiS's referendum questions in 2023 instead of walking past the ballot
box. One of those questions was the retirement age. That is why our people can
stand in a defence debate and talk about pensions without being laughed at.?]

- @safe_veto_override
- @safe_veto_workaround
- @safe_veto_social_floor
- @safe_veto_campaign

@safe_veto_override
title: Attempt the override and force every deputy onto the record
subtitle: Almost certainly fails; it produces a roll call that follows the right into the 2027 campaign.
on-arrival: {!
Q.safe_veto_response = "Override attempted";
Q.parliament_visibility =
    (Number(Q.parliament_visibility) || 40) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.president_relation =
    (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) - 6;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 6;
Q.konf_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.1;
Q.defence_readiness =
    (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 45) + 1;
Q.public_mood_pending_national_security_support += 7;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "The override fails and the defence roll call is published in full";
!}

The vote is lost, as the whips said it would be. What it produces is a list:
every deputy who declined to fund air defence, printed against their
constituency, available to anyone who wants to use it for the next eighteen
months.

Konfederacja's deputies are on it and are entirely comfortable being on it,
which is a reminder that the anti-rearmament position now has an electorate of
its own. The equipment is still not ordered.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the override roll call

@safe_veto_workaround
title: Rebuild the financing inside the budget act the President cannot easily block
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Gets the money moving through a constitutionally awkward route the Tribunal may examine.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No fiscal or legal capacity is free to redraft the financing route.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.safe_veto_response = "Budget-act route";
Q.defence_readiness =
    (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 45) + 7;
Q.eu_relations = (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 47) + 3;
Q.administrative_capacity =
    (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.constitutional_restraint = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) - 5
);
Q.constitutional_conflict_level =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_conflict_level) || 0) + 6;
Q.president_relation =
    (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) - 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_national_security_support += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Defence financing is rewritten into the budget act and the contracts proceed";
!}

The President's veto on the budget act is constitutionally constrained in a way
his ordinary veto is not, so the financing is rebuilt inside it. The contracts
are signed, the firms restart, and the delivery schedule survives.

The method is a stretch and the Palace's lawyers say so immediately. We have
answered an abuse of the veto with an aggressive reading of the budget
procedure, and the Tribunal now has an invitation to rule on both. The
equipment arrives; the precedent is available to every future government
looking for a route around a president.

- @poland_event_queue: Move the financing into the budget act

@safe_veto_social_floor
# The 2023 referendum's fourth question was the retirement age. A party that
# contested the questions instead of joining the boycott owns that argument
# three years later, when rearmament money is being weighed against pensions.
title: Offer the votes in exchange for a written social floor beside the loans
